{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9beafc74f8043863","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9008 (Make RHOAI more usable for enterprise teams)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Result\n13\t\n14\tNot triaged as below-threshold or docs-only. The strategy contains three genuine\n15\tunknowns (its own Open Questions table) whose answers change which downstream\n16\tepics exist and what they do, and the scope spans two components\n17\t(Dashboard, Notebooks) owned by two teams. Full decomposition follows.\n18\t\n19\t## Strategy Health (parsed structure)\n20\t\n21\tSections present: Problem Statement, High-Level Requirements, Affected\n22\tComponents, Out of Scope, Open Questions.\n23\t\n24\tSections **missing** (health warnings, decomposition proceeded with available\n25\tinformation):\n26\t\n27\t- Impacted Teams table (owner teams derived from architecture context)\n28\t- Dependencies table\n29\t- Acceptance Criteria (no Given/When/Then; per-epic ACs below are derived from\n30\t  HLRs and standard implementation requirements)\n31\t- Non-Functional Requirements\n32\t- Staff Engineer Input\n33\t\n34\t## Epic List\n35\t\n36\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n37\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E001 | Resolve enterprise admin-configuration direction conflict | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E002 | Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E003 | Identify target enterprise tools and integration scope | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E004 | Enterprise admin configuration experience | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E005 | Data-scientist onboarding experience in the console | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E006 | Workbench readiness for day-one onboarding | Implementation | Workbenches | Notebooks | P1 |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E007 | Enterprise tooling integration | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E008 | Enterprise usability best practices whitepaper | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P2 |\n46\t\n47\t## Dependency DAG\n48\t\n49\t```mermaid\n50\tgraph TD\n51\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9008-E001: Resolve admin-config direction]\n52\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9008-E002: Define onboarding scope and baseline]\n53\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-9008-E003: Identify enterprise tools]\n54\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-9008-E004: Admin configuration experience]\n55\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-9008-E005: Onboarding experience in console]\n56\t    E006[RHAISTRAT-9008-E006: Workbench readiness]\n57\t    E007[RHAISTRAT-9008-E007: Enterprise tooling integration]\n58\t    E008[RHAISTRAT-9008-E008: Usability whitepaper]\n59\t    E001 --> E004\n60\t    E002 --> E005\n61\t    E002 --> E006\n62\t    E003 --> E007\n63\t    E004 --> E008\n64\t    E005 --> E008\n65\t    E006 --> E008\n66\t    E007 --> E008\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t## DAG Justification\n70\t\n71\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n72\t|------|------|-----------|\n73\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The HLR-1 direction conflict (fewer exposed options vs. more fine-grained per-project controls) determines what the admin-configuration implementation builds. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n74\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | Onboarding scope (cluster access / project setup / first workbench / first deployed model) determines which console friction points the implementation addresses. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n75\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 3 | Same scope decision determines which workbench-layer (Notebooks) friction items are in scope. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n76\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 3 | No enterprise tools are named in the strategy; the integration epic's existence and scope depend on the identified tool list. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n77\t| E004 → E008 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Whitepaper describes delivered usability improvements; blocked by all Implementation epics. |\n78\t| E005 → E008 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n79\t| E006 → E008 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n80\t| E007 → E008 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n81\t| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 ∥ E003 | Rule 14 / independent unknowns | The three open questions are independent of each other; investigations run in parallel. |\n82\t| (no edge) E004 ∥ E005 ∥ E006 ∥ E007 (post-gate) | Rules 14/15 | Implementations in different components/repos or different areas; no shared build-against artifacts. |\n83\t\n84\tdocs-authoring priority exception applied to E008: strategy frontmatter\n85\t`priority: Normal` → P2. It does not push priority upstream.\n86\t\n87\t## Investigation Treatment of Open Questions\n88\t\n89\t| Open question (from strategy) | Changes which epics exist / what they do? | Handling |\n90\t|---|---|---|\n91\t| 1. Which accounts' feedback takes precedence for HLR-1 (conflicting directions)? | Yes — determines the scope of the admin-configuration implementation | Investigation epic E001, gating E004 |\n92\t| 2. What does \"onboarding\" cover for HLR-2? | Yes — determines which onboarding implementations exist and what they target | Investigation epic E002, gating E005 and E006 |\n93\t| 3. Which enterprise tools does HLR-3 mean? | Yes — determines whether integration epics exist, for which tools, and on which components | Investigation epic E003, gating E007 |\n94\t\n95\t**No conditional branch files were emitted.** Although HLR-1's conflict has two\n96\tstated poles, the resolution space is not bounded to ≤3 enumerable\n97\tepic-structure outcomes (a reconciliation — e.g. tiered defaults plus advanced\n98\tper-project controls — would satisfy both accounts and change scope rather than\n99\tselect between two pre-drawn structures). The gating is therefore modeled with\n100\t`gated_by` + `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on each downstream\n101\timplementation rather than branch epics.\n102\t\n103\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n104\t\n105\t| HLR | Priority (strategy) | Epics | Coverage |\n106\t|-----|--------------------|-------|----------|\n107\t| HLR-1 — Administration should be simpler (conflicting directions) | — (unspecified) | E001, E004 | Investigation + gated implementation |\n108\t| HLR-2 — New data-scientist onboarding under a day (scope undefined) | — (unspecified) | E002, E005, E006 | Investigation + gated implementations (console + workbench layers) |\n109\t| HLR-3 — Better integration with enterprise tooling (tools unnamed) | — (unspecified) | E003, E007 | Investigation + gated implementation |\n110\t| HLR-4 — Publish enterprise usability best practices whitepaper | P2 | E008 | docs-authoring epic |\n111\t\n112\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n113\t\n114\t**Priority defaults:** HLR-1/2/3 carry no priority in the strategy. They were\n115\tdefaulted to **P1** based on the problem statement's \"Leadership wants visible\n116\tusability progress this release\". This default must be confirmed by the strategy\n117\towner (see Health Warnings).\n118\t\n119\t## Component Mapping Notes\n120\t\n121\t- Strategy's Affected Components are a bare list (no change descriptions, no\n122\t  owners). Both map directly to canonical components: **Dashboard** and\n123\t  **Notebooks**.\n124\t- Owner teams derived from architecture context: Dashboard → **RHOAI Dashboard**;\n125\t  Notebooks → **Workbenches**.\n126\t- E007 (enterprise tooling integration) is assigned to **Dashboard** as a\n127\t  placeholder: the affected component cannot be known until the tool\n128\t  identification investigation resolves. Reassign if the identified tools point\n129\t  elsewhere (captured in its gate failure impact).\n130\t- E008 (whitepaper) maps to the canonical **Documentation** component; the\n131\t  owning team is not stated anywhere in the strategy (Impacted Teams table\n132\t  missing) and was set to RHOAI Documentation — confirm with strategy owner.\n133\t- E002 is assigned to the RHOAI Dashboard team because onboarding is a\n134\t  cross-component journey whose console surface the Dashboard team owns; the\n135\t  workbench-side follow-through lives in E006 (Workbenches team).\n136\t\n137\t## Health Warnings\n138\t\n139\t1. **Contradictory requirement (HLR-1):** one account wants fewer exposed\n140\t   configuration options, another wants more fine-grained per-project controls.\n141\t   Not resolvable by decomposition; gated on Investigation E001.\n142\t2. **Unmeasurable acceptance target (HLR-2):** \"less than a day\" cannot be\n143\t   tested until onboarding scope is defined and a baseline measured (E002).\n144\t   Scope trap if implementation epics were created without the gate.\n145\t3. **Unprioritized HLRs:** HLR-1/2/3 have no priority. Defaulted to P1 from the\n146\t   leadership-urgency statement; confirm.\n147\t4. **Vague requirement (HLR-3):** no enterprise tools named; \"integrate better\"\n148\t   is undefined. E007's component assignment is a placeholder pending E003.\n149\t5. **Missing strategy sections:** Impacted Teams, Dependencies table,\n150\t   Acceptance Criteria, NFRs — per-epic ACs are derived from HLRs plus standard\n151\t   implementation requirements; they are necessarily thinner than\n152\t   strategy-provided Given/When/Then ACs would be.\n153\t6. **No explicit out-of-scope boundary:** \"Nothing has been explicitly scoped\n154\t   out.\" Boundary risk for the integration epic in particular (enterprise\n155\t   tooling could expand indefinitely); E003's deliverable includes a bounded,\n156\t   prioritized recommendation.\n157\t7. **Unconsolidated feedback source:** the problem statement notes feedback\n158\t   arrived through different channels and is partially contradictory; all three\n159\t   investigations include feedback consolidation as a deliverable.\n160\t\n161\t## Tiered Delivery\n162\t\n163\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing. All uncertainty\n164\tis internal (requirement definition), handled via Investigation gates.\n165\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a4f73abddbdb7c1","agent_id":"a86705923f9f1b1ce","session_id":"cc08ccf1-892e-454d-8ed1-68ebd3e76220","uuid":"caecbbe5-275c-418d-bf92-967d2b1fc543","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:44:11.515Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9beafc74f8043863","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
