{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-868903b75aea200f","type":"tool_result","content":"===== RHAISTRAT-9008-E001.md =====\n---\nepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\ntitle: Resolve enterprise admin-configuration direction conflict\nparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\ncomponent: Dashboard\nteam: RHOAI Dashboard\ntype: Investigation\npriority: P1\ninvestigation_signals:\n  question_specificity: 1\n  source_accessibility: 0\n  local_runnability: 1\n  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n  human_judgment_required: -2\nimplementation_type: null\ndependencies: []\nai_signals: null\nai_implementability: Medium\nai_implementability_score: 0\njira_key: null\nbranch: null\ngated_by: null\ngate_failure_impact: null\n---\n# Resolve enterprise admin-configuration direction conflict\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the conflicting enterprise feedback on administrative\nsimplicity: one strategic account wants fewer configuration options exposed\n(\"too many knobs\"), while another explicitly wants more fine-grained controls\nper project. It consolidates the unconsolidated feedback, establishes which\ndirection (or reconciliation of both) takes precedence, and produces a decision\nthat the admin-configuration implementation work builds against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate the enterprise account feedback about administrative\n  configuration from all channels through which it arrived, resolving the\n  partial contradictions documented in the strategy.\n- Determine whose feedback takes precedence and on what basis (account tier,\n  product strategy alignment, feasibility), or whether both can be satisfied\n  through a tiered design (e.g. simple defaults with advanced per-project\n  controls available on demand).\n- Identify the specific configuration surfaces in the RHOAI console that each\n  direction concerns (against Dashboard and OdhDashboardConfig capabilities\n  described in architecture context).\n- Produce a written decision record: the chosen direction, the affected\n  configuration surfaces, and recommended scope for the implementation work.\n- Flag any identified friction points that fall outside the Dashboard component\n  for handoff.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All known enterprise feedback on administrative configuration is collected\n  into one place, with sources and contradictions made explicit.\n- A decision is recorded on which direction takes precedence, or a concrete\n  reconciliation that satisfies both accounts, with rationale.\n- The decision enumerates the configuration surfaces it applies to.\n- The decision is confirmed with the strategy owner / product stakeholders\n  before implementation begins.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 — Administration should be simpler (accounts request conflicting\n  directions: fewer exposed options vs. more fine-grained per-project controls).\n===== RHAISTRAT-9008-E002.md =====\n---\nepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\ntitle: Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline\nparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\ncomponent: Dashboard\nteam: RHOAI Dashboard\ntype: Investigation\npriority: P1\ninvestigation_signals:\n  question_specificity: 1\n  source_accessibility: 1\n  local_runnability: 1\n  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n  human_judgment_required: -1\nimplementation_type: null\ndependencies: []\nai_signals: null\nai_implementability: Medium\nai_implementability_score: 1\njira_key: null\nbranch: null\ngated_by: null\ngate_failure_impact: null\n---\n# Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation defines what \"onboarding a new data scientist\" covers and\nestablishes where the time is currently spent, so that the \"less than a day\"\ntarget becomes measurable and the right onboarding improvements get built. It\nis a cross-component journey spanning the console (Dashboard) and the workbench\nlayer (Notebooks).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Decide the onboarding boundary: which of cluster access, project setup, first\n  workbench, and first deployed model (the strategy's open question) count as\n  \"onboarding a new data scientist\".\n- Map the current onboarding journey end to end and measure (or estimate from\n  representative trials) where elapsed time and friction occur today.\n- Identify which friction points fall in the console and which in the workbench\n  / notebook-server layer, so the follow-up work can be assigned to the right\n  teams.\n- Define a measurable success metric for the \"less than a day\" target under the\n  chosen boundary (e.g. time-to-first-successful-workbench, time-to-first-model\n  for a representative new user persona).\n- Produce a written scope decision and prioritized friction list.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The onboarding boundary is decided and recorded, covering the strategy's open\n  question (cluster access, project setup, first workbench, first deployed\n  model).\n- A baseline of where onboarding time is spent today exists, with method and\n  limitations noted.\n- The success metric for \"less than a day\" is operationalized and measurable.\n- Friction items are split by owning area (console vs. workbench layer).\n- The scope decision is confirmed with the strategy owner before implementation\n  begins.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 — Onboarding a new data scientist should take \"less than a day\"\n  (currently undefined what onboarding includes or where the day is spent).\n===== RHAISTRAT-9008-E003.md =====\n---\nepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E003\ntitle: Identify target enterprise tools and integration scope\nparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\ncomponent: Dashboard\nteam: RHOAI Dashboard\ntype: Investigation\npriority: P1\ninvestigation_signals:\n  question_specificity: 0\n  source_accessibility: 0\n  local_runnability: 0\n  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n  human_judgment_required: -2\nimplementation_type: null\ndependencies: []\nai_signals: null\nai_implementability: Low\nai_implementability_score: -2\njira_key: null\nbranch: null\ngated_by: null\ngate_failure_impact: null\n---\n# Identify target enterprise tools and integration scope\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation identifies which enterprise tools the consolidated feedback\nrefers to and what \"integrate better\" concretely means for each, producing a\nbounded, prioritized integration recommendation. The strategy names no specific\ntools, so no integration work can be scoped until this resolves.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate the enterprise account feedback to extract the specific tools and\n  tool categories behind \"integrate better with existing enterprise tooling\".\n- For each candidate tool, determine the integration form that would deliver\n  the value (e.g. authentication/SSO, identity/group sync, source control,\n  CI/CD, monitoring/observability, data governance) at a capability level —\n  without committing to specific API designs.\n- Identify which RHOAI component each integration would touch (Dashboard,\n  Notebooks, or another component) so the implementation work lands with the\n  right team.\n- Assess feasibility and rough effort per candidate integration.\n- Produce a bounded, prioritized recommendation of which integrations to pursue\n  this release, with the affected components and an explicit not-pursuing list\n  (the strategy has no out-of-scope boundary — this provides one).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A consolidated list of the enterprise tools the feedback actually refers to\n  exists, with sources.\n- Each candidate integration has a described integration form, affected RHOAI\n  component, and feasibility assessment.\n- A prioritized, bounded recommendation identifies what is pursued this release\n  and what is explicitly deferred.\n- The recommendation is confirmed with the strategy owner before implementation\n  begins.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 — The platform should \"integrate better\" with existing enterprise\n  tooling (no specific tools named in the consolidated feedback).\n===== RHAISTRAT-9008-E004.md =====\n---\nepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E004\ntitle: Enterprise admin configuration experience\nparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\ncomponent: Dashboard\nteam: RHOAI Dashboard\ntype: Implementation\npriority: P1\ndependencies:\n- RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\ngated_by: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\ngate_failure_impact:\n  action: rewrite\n  fallback_approach: If the direction conflict cannot be resolved, re-scope this epic\n    to whichever direction the strategy owner confirms, or split into separate epics\n    per direction if both are pursued independently.\nai_signals:\n  change_specificity: -1\n  pattern_precedent: 1\n  adapter_pattern: 0\n  existing_foundation: 1\n  open_questions: -1\n  external_dependency: 0\n  human_process_gates: -1\n  repo_access: 1\n  architecture_claims: 0\nimplementation_type: null\ninvestigation_signals: null\nai_implementability: Medium\nai_implementability_score: 0\njira_key: null\nbranch: null\n---\n# Enterprise admin configuration experience\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the administrative configuration experience chosen by the\npreceding investigation into the conflicting enterprise feedback: either the\nsimplified configuration surface, the fine-grained per-project controls, or a\nreconciliation of both. The Dashboard is the console surface for per-component\nfeature flags and defaults (via the OdhDashboardConfig CR) and is where\nadministrators interact with configuration today.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the configuration-experience direction recorded in the\n  investigation's decision (simplification, granularity, or tiered\n  combination), across the configuration surfaces the decision enumerates.\n- Cover the relevant console surfaces for administering configuration\n  defaults and per-project overrides.\n- Include incidental documentation touch-ups (updated captions, labels, or\n  references in existing admin docs) that fall out of the same change — no new\n  doc topics are authored here.\n- Validate the experience against representative administrator personas from\n  the consolidated enterprise feedback.\n\nExact scope is finalized from the investigation's decision record; do not\npre-commit to specific settings or UI structures beyond what it specifies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The configuration experience matches the direction and surfaces enumerated in\n  the investigation's confirmed decision.\n- An administrator from the \"too many knobs\" account persona can complete\n  representative configuration tasks with fewer exposed options (or the\n  equivalent chosen direction), verified by the success measure the decision\n  defines.\n- An administrator from the fine-grained-controls persona retains the control\n  the decision requires (or the reconciliation satisfies both), verified\n  likewise.\n- The change does not remove capability required by existing users that the\n  decision did not authorize removing.\n- Incidental doc touch-ups from the same change are included.\n- Because this work may replace existing admin configuration behavior: a\n  rollback path or feature flag allows reverting to the current experience.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 — Administration should be simpler (conflicting directions: fewer\n  exposed options vs. more fine-grained per-project controls).\n===== RHAISTRAT-9008-E005.md =====\n---\nepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E005\ntitle: Data-scientist onboarding experience in the console\nparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\ncomponent: Dashboard\nteam: RHOAI Dashboard\ntype: Implementation\npriority: P1\ndependencies:\n- RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\ngated_by: RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\ngate_failure_impact:\n  action: rewrite\n  fallback_approach: If onboarding scope excludes console-surface stages, remove this\n    epic; if the boundary shifts, rewrite scope to the newly prioritized console friction\n    items.\nai_signals:\n  change_specificity: -1\n  pattern_precedent: 1\n  adapter_pattern: 0\n  existing_foundation: 1\n  open_questions: -1\n  external_dependency: 0\n  human_process_gates: 0\n  repo_access: 1\n  architecture_claims: 0\nimplementation_type: null\ninvestigation_signals: null\nai_implementability: Medium\nai_implementability_score: 1\njira_key: null\nbranch: null\n---\n# Data-scientist onboarding experience in the console\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the console-side improvements that bring new data-scientist\nonboarding under the boundary and time target defined by the preceding\nonboarding-scope investigation. It covers the friction items the investigation\nassigned to the console: the project-creation, workbench-spawn, and\ngetting-started surfaces of the Dashboard.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the console friction items prioritized in the investigation's\n  scope decision (expected areas: getting to a first workbench, project setup\n  steps surfaced in the console, and first-use guidance), exactly as that\n  decision bounds them.\n- Wire the console surfaces to existing component backends as needed; the\n  Dashboard reads and writes CRs and owns no data plane.\n- Include incidental documentation touch-ups (captions, screenshots,\n  references in existing docs) that fall out of the same change — no new\n  tutorials or doc topics are authored here.\n\nExact scope is finalized from the investigation's decision record.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The console friction items the investigation prioritized are addressed, with\n  no scope beyond its boundary.\n- A representative new data scientist can complete the defined onboarding\n  journey's console portion within the operationalized time target measured by\n  the investigation's metric, verified in a trial with representative users.\n- No regression to existing project, workbench, or serving console workflows.\n- Incidental doc touch-ups from the same change are included.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 — Onboarding a new data scientist should take \"less than a day\" (scope\n  and time baseline defined by the preceding investigation).\n===== RHAISTRAT-9008-E00