ge_specificity:\n-1` / `open_questions: -1` on all gated implementations.\n\nTwo signal values are arguable because they are inconsistent with the treatment\nof structurally identical epics: E004 and E007 score\n`human_process_gates: -1` partly on grounds that apply equally to E005/E006,\nwhich score 0. E004's rationale cites the direction-decision stakeholder\nconfirmation — but that confirmation is E001's acceptance criterion and has\nalready passed by the time E004 runs; E005 is gated by the identical\nstructure (E002's \"scope decision is confirmed with the strategy owner\") yet\nscores 0. E004 and E007 also cite representative-user validation as a human\napproval step, while E005's rationale explicitly classifies the same kind of\nvalidation as \"an acceptance activity, not a process gate\" (score 0). E007\nadditionally cites the recommendation's strategy-owner confirmation, which is\nE003's AC, not E007's. Either E004/E007 should be 0 or E005/E006 should be -1 —\nthe same gating-plus-user-validation structure must score the same way. This\ndoes not change any epic's band enough to alter `ai_implementability` outcomes\nmaterially, so it is minor.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria. Rule-mandated ACs are present where\napplicable: E004 (which may replace existing admin configuration behavior) has\nan explicit rollback/feature-flag AC; E008 (docs-authoring) has the technical\nreview AC plus publication through the docs process; no konflux-chain epics\nexist so the build-pipeline AC does not apply. The strategy provides no ACs of\nits own, and the per-epic ACs are correctly anchored to the gating\ninvestigations' decision records (e.g., \"matches the direction and surfaces\nenumerated in the investigation's confirmed decision\") rather than inventing\nunsupported specifics — this is disclosed in the health warnings. No epic body\nreferences sibling epics by bare draft ID; all references use full\nRHAISTRAT-90