{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8a51e96b2158ab","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9008 (Make RHOAI more usable for enterprise teams)\n10\t\n11\t## Triage Result\n12\t\n13\tNot triaged as below-threshold or docs-only. The strategy contains three genuine\n14\tunknowns (its own Open Questions table) whose answers change which downstream\n15\tepics exist and what they do, and the scope spans two components\n16\t(Dashboard, Notebooks) owned by two teams. Full decomposition follows.\n17\t\n18\t## Strategy Health (parsed structure)\n19\t\n20\tSections present: Problem Statement, High-Level Requirements, Affected\n21\tComponents, Out of Scope, Open Questions.\n22\t\n23\tSections **missing** (health warnings, decomposition proceeded with available\n24\tinformation):\n25\t\n26\t- Impacted Teams table (owner teams derived from architecture context)\n27\t- Dependencies table\n28\t- Acceptance Criteria (no Given/When/Then; per-epic ACs below are derived from\n29\t  HLRs and standard implementation requirements)\n30\t- Non-Functional Requirements\n31\t- Staff Engineer Input\n32\t\n33\t## Epic List\n34\t\n35\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n36\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E001 | Resolve enterprise admin-configuration direction conflict | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E002 | Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E003 | Identify target enterprise tools and integration scope | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E004 | Enterprise admin configuration experience | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard |