\n47\t  for a representative new user persona).\n48\t- Produce a written scope decision and prioritized friction list.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- The onboarding boundary is decided and recorded, covering the strategy's open\n53\t  question (cluster access, project setup, first workbench, first deployed\n54\t  model).\n55\t- A baseline of where onboarding time is spent today exists, with method and\n56\t  limitations noted.\n57\t- The success metric for \"less than a day\" is operationalized and measurable.\n58\t- Friction items are split by owning area (console vs. workbench layer).\n59\t- The scope decision is confirmed with the strategy owner before implementation\n60\t  begins.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 — Onboarding a new data scientist should take \"less than a day\"\n65\t  (currently undefined what onboarding includes or where the day is spent).\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fb09261067101a","agent_id":"a2ffe5240e4caaf98","session_id":"cc08ccf1-892e-454d-8ed1-68ebd3e76220","uuid":"5ccdbdf9-b916-405b-b0c9-70de2d4193d5","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:50:51.994Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa23fab69178c711","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
