{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0e87bf36097ecfa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\n3\ttitle: Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Define data-scientist onboarding scope and time baseline\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation defines what \"onboarding a new data scientist\" covers and\n30\testablishes where the time is currently spent, so that the \"less than a day\"\n31\ttarget becomes measurable and the right onboarding improvements get built. It\n32\tis a cross-component journey spanning the console (Dashboard) and the workbench\n33\tlayer (Notebooks).\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Decide the onboarding boundary: which of cluster access, project setup, first\n38\t  workbench, and first deployed model (the strategy's open question) count as\n39\t  \"onboarding a new data scientist\".\n40\t- Map the current onboarding journey end to end and measure (or estimate from\n41\t  representative trials) where elapsed time and friction occur today.\n42\t- Identify which friction points fall in the console and which in the workbench\n43\t  / notebook-server layer, so the follow-up work can be assigned to the right\n44\t  teams.\n45\t- Define a measurable success metric for the \"less than a day\" target under the\n46\t  chosen boundary (e.g. time-to-first-successful-workbench, time-to-first-model\n47\t  for a representative new user persona).\n48\t- Verify the chosen boundary against the downstream epic structure: the\n49\t  follow-up implementation work covers a console layer (Dashboard) and a\n50\t  workbench layer (Notebooks) — the strategy's Affected Components. If the\n51\t  boundary includes a stage whose friction is not absorbed by either layer\n52\t  (notably \"first deployed model\", whose friction would fall to model-serving\n53\t  surfaces outside the two affected components), the scope decision must say\n54\t  so explicitly and route that friction to a separate follow-up strategy\n55\t  rather than leaving it unowned.\n56\t- Produce a written scope decision and prioritized friction list.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The onboarding boundary is decided and recorded, covering the strategy's open\n61\t  question (cluster access, project setup, first workbench, first deployed\n62\t  model).\n63\t- A baseline of where onboarding time is spent today exists, with method and\n64\t  limitations noted.\n65\t- The success metric for \"less than a day\" is operationalized and measurable.\n66\t- Friction items are split by owning area (console vs. workbench layer).\n67\t- If the chosen boundary includes stages outside the console/workbench layers\n68\t  (e.g. first deployed model on serving surfaces), those friction items are\n69\t  explicitly routed to a separate follow-up strategy, with none left unowned.\n70\t- The scope decision is confirmed with the strategy owner before implementation\n71\t  begins.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-2 — Onboarding a new data scientist should take \"less than a day\"\n76\t  (currently undefined what onboarding includes or where the day is spent).\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-854b3bc7d232f952","agent_id":"a465806246728c774","session_id":"cc08ccf1-892e-454d-8ed1-68ebd3e76220","uuid":"d46f2c10-2569-4ebb-9160-71e2a2a9fe07","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:54:03.025Z","tool_result_me