{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae47511d40bf5f6b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E003\n3\ttitle: Identify target enterprise tools and integration scope\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 0\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Identify target enterprise tools and integration scope\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation identifies which enterprise tools the consolidated feedback\n30\trefers to and what \"integrate better\" concretely means for each, producing a\n31\tbounded, prioritized integration recommendation. The strategy names no specific\n32\ttools, so no integration work can be scoped until this resolves.\n33\t\n34\t## Scope\n35\t\n36\t- Consolidate the enterprise account feedback to extract the specific tools and\n37\t  tool categories behind \"integrate better with existing enterprise tooling\".\n38\t- For each candidate tool, determine the integration form that would deliver\n39\t  the value (e.g. authentication/SSO, identity/group sync, source control,\n40\t  CI/CD, monitoring/observability, data governance) at a capability level —\n41\t  without committing to specific API designs.\n42\t- Identify which RHOAI component each integration would touch (Dashboard,\n43\t  Notebooks, or another component) so the implementation work lands with the\n44\t  right team. Where an assignment differs from the component initially\n45\t  assigned to the integration implementation work (a placeholder pending this\n46\t  investigation's outcome), the recommendation must flag the reassignment\n47\t  explicitly so the affected epic is moved to the correct owning team rather\n48\t  than left on the placeholder.\n49\t- Assess feasibility and rough effort per candidate integration.\n50\t- Produce a bounded, prioritized recommendation of which integrations to pursue\n51\t  this release, with the affected components and an explicit not-pursuing list\n52\t  (the strategy has no out-of-scope boundary — this provides one).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A consolidated list of the enterprise tools the feedback actually refers to\n57\t  exists, with sources.\n58\t- Each candidate integration has a described integration form, affected RHOAI\n59\t  component, and feasibility assessment.\n60\t- A prioritized, bounded recommendation identifies what is pursued this release\n61\t  and what is explicitly deferred.\n62\t- Any component/team reassignment of the integration implementation work away\n63\t  from its initial placeholder assignment is stated explicitly in the\n64\t  recommendation.\n65\t- The recommendation is confirmed with the strategy owner before implementation\n66\t  begins.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-3 — The platform should \"integrate better\" with existing enterprise\n71\t  tooling (no specific tools named in the consolidated feedback).\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-854b3bc7d232f952","agent_id":"a465806246728c774","session_id":"cc08ccf1-892e-454d-8ed1-68ebd3e76220","uuid":"88a8dbe7-1245-4398-aed1-35ee149ea26d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:54:19.861Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae47511d40bf5f6b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9008"}
